      "body": "<!--e57a25ab6845829454e8d69fc972939a-->\n\nThe following sections might be updated with supplementary metadata relevant to reviewers and maintainers.\n\n<!--006a51241073e994b41acfe9ec718e94-->\n### External sites\n\n* Code coverage & benchmarks: https://corecheck.dev/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36629\n* Ralph review <img src=https://review.fish.foo/assets/bitcoin/bitcoin/36629.png alt=\"Ralph review status\"> https://git.fish.foo/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36629#author-ralph\n<!--021abf342d371248e50ceaed478a90ca-->\n### Reviews\nSee [the guideline](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-review) and [AI policy](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/AI_POLICY.md) for information on the review process.\n| Type | Reviewers |\n| ---- | --------- |\n| Concept ACK | [sedited](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36629#issuecomment-6372429119), [l0rinc](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36629#issuecomment-6372628097) |\n\nIf your review is incorrectly listed, please copy-paste <code>&lt;!--meta-tag:bot-skip--&gt;</code> into the comment that the bot should ignore.\n<!--5faf32d7da4f0f540f40219e4f7537a3-->\n### LLM Linter (✨ experimental)\n\n\n\nPossible places where named args for integral literals may be used (e.g. `func(x, /*named_arg=*/0)` in C++, and `func(x, named_arg=0)` in Python):\n\n- `src/init.cpp`: `std::make_unique<TxoScriptIndex>(interfaces::MakeChain(node), index_cache_sizes.txoscript_index, false, do_reindex)`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, -1, 95, remaining_bytes)`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 95, 90, remaining_bytes)`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 0, 102, remaining_bytes)`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 0, 100, remaining_bytes)`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 1, 1, remaining_bytes)` in `check_read_error`\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 1, 2, remaining_bytes)` in the false-positive budget test\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 1, 1, remaining_bytes)` in the boundary-key budget check\n- `src/test/txoscriptindex_tests.cpp`: `index.Find(script_hash, 1, 1, remaining_bytes)` in the exact-budget check\n\n\n\n\nPossible places where comparison-specific test macros should replace generic comparisons:\n\n- `src/test/ordered_varint_tests.cpp`: The `BOOST_CHECK_THROW` checks for truncated encodings, invalid prefixes, oversized values, and uint32 overflow only verify `std::ios_base::failure`. Prefer `BOOST_CHECK_EXCEPTION` with a reason matcher to verify the expected error message.\n- `test/functional/rpc_getscripthistory.py`: `assert output is spent` → `assert_equal(output, spent)`.\n- `test/functional/rpc_getscripthistory.py`: `assert sum(sizes[:53]) + sum(sizes[:10]) > limit` → `assert_greater_than(sum(sizes[:53]) + sum(sizes[:10]), limit)`.\n\n\n\n<sup>2026-10-23 17:40:54</sup>\n",
